 "Bopomofo is not an alternative Chinese script. It is a sound notation, like a phonetic alphabet, with its own symbols.": 1,
 "Bopomofo uses 37 dedicated symbols instead of Latin letters, so it avoids existing reading reflexes — which suits families connected to Taiwan and children who already read fluently.": 1,
 "In practice ㄅ writes the b sound, ㄆ the aspirated p, ㄚ the vowel a. A Chinese character is then read as one or two blocks plus a tone. The system has 21 initials and 16 finals: 37 symbols to recognise before any syllable can be read.": 1,
 "The advantage over pinyin is the absence of interference. A child who already reads a Latin script sees \"qi\" or \"xie\" and applies familiar reading rules automatically, and the error settles in. With unfamiliar symbols there is no reflex to correct.": 1,
 "The drawback is practical: bopomofo is used mainly in Taiwan. Elsewhere there is less material, and typing requires a specific keyboard layout. The choice therefore depends on family context and school. Lumi Bopomofo teaches the system with tracing, sound and tones, free to start and with no ads.": 1,
